# Deploy package versioning

Deployable packages (`backend`, `web`, `marketing`, `admin`) version **independently** in each package's `package.json`. Shared libs (`shared-types`, `ui`, `email-templates`, `db-admin`) stay at `0.0.0`; their changes require **consumer** version bumps.

## When to bump

- **Before `git push`** to `staging` or `main` — not on every commit.
- Multiple local commits are fine; one version-bump commit before push covers the whole push range.

## Local workflow

```bash
pnpm setup:hooks   # once per clone — enables .githooks/pre-push

# ... feature commits without version bumps ...

pnpm bump:versions              # interactive: patch / minor / major per package
git add packages/*/package.json
git commit -m "chore(repo)[#N]: bump versions for push"

bash scripts/with-ci-env.sh pnpm lint && ...   # full CI gate (rule 06)
git push origin staging
```

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `pnpm bump:versions` | Detect changed deployables + shared-lib consumers; bump `package.json` after confirm |
| `pnpm bump:versions --dry-run` | Show proposed bumps without writing |
| `pnpm check:push-version-bumps` | Manual pre-push check (upstream..HEAD) |
| `pnpm setup:hooks` | Install pre-push version gate |

## Pre-push gate

`.githooks/pre-push` runs `scripts/check-push-version-bumps.mjs` on pushes to `staging`/`main`. It compares **remote..local** (all commits being pushed). If deploy-relevant source changed but semver did not increase → push blocked.

On failure, stderr includes **`pnpm bump:versions`** — use that script to fix.

Escape (operator only): `SKIP_DEPLOY_VERSION_BUMP_CHECK=1 git push --no-verify`

## Shared-lib → consumer map

| Shared package | Bump these deployables |
|---|---|
| `shared-types` | backend, web, marketing, admin |
| `ui` | web, marketing |
| `email-templates` | backend |
| `db-admin` | admin |

## Agent obligations

When pushing deployable code to `staging`:

1. Run `pnpm bump:versions` (or bump `package.json` manually) if the push includes deploy-relevant changes.
2. Commit version bumps in a separate commit before push.
3. Run full CI gate (rule `06-local-ci-before-commit.mdc`).
4. Push — pre-push hook validates the push range.

**No Changesets.** No per-commit version requirement. CI does not auto-bump versions.
